# General engineering baseline

- **Read before writing.** Match the naming, layout, formatter and linter the repo already uses before applying a preference of your own.
- **Smallest change that solves the task.** No drive-by refactors; a new dependency needs a reason in the PR.
- **Tests travel with the change.** A behavior change changes a test; a bug fix starts with a failing one.
- **No secrets in git.** Keys, tokens and `.env` files stay out of commits and logs (see `git-secrets-safety`).
- **Errors are handled or surfaced,** never swallowed. Log context, not payloads that hold personal data.
- **Names carry intent;** comments say why, not what.
- **Docs follow behavior.** README, CHANGELOG and ADRs change in the same PR as the behavior they describe.
- **Branching:** staging first, never `main` (see `cursor-skills-git-workflow`).
- Stack rules (`cursor-skills-<stack>`) load by file glob; follow them on top of this one.
